WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.831
Some secrets wait five hundred years. This
one was broken twice in a single autumn,

00:00:07.831 --> 00:00:10.571
by two codebreakers working separately.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.126
Autumn, 1496. Maximilian, King of the Romans,

00:00:16.126 --> 00:00:21.203
has come into Italy with the Holy
League, at war with Florence.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.352
Camped at Pisa, he needs
money, men and allies.

00:00:25.352 --> 00:00:28.347
He puts his terms to the orators of Siena.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.608
His secretary, Niklas
Ziegler, writes them down,

00:00:32.608 --> 00:00:37.224
and every word that matters goes
into a cipher of invented signs.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.184
Sixty signs. Some stand for
letters, some for doubled letters,

00:00:46.184 --> 00:00:50.571
and some for nothing at all: dots
and bars, thrown in to mislead.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.266
In the modern catalogue the
pages had no sender, no receiver,

00:00:56.266 --> 00:00:58.505
and only a guess at the century.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.217
In September 2026, this project
broke it with a search. Guess a key,

00:01:07.217 --> 00:01:10.286
score the Latin, improve it, and repeat.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.753
A month later, George
Lasry, working with Claude,

00:01:14.753 --> 00:01:17.076
broke it again from the other side.

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:21.789
The clear Latin around the cipher
words suggested what they had to say.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.945
Neither used the other's
key. Both read the same line:

00:01:26.945 --> 00:01:30.160
that the Sienese lend the King 5,000 ducats.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.199
Then the two keys were laid side by side.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.426
38 letter signs. 35 give
the same letter in both.

00:01:47.426 --> 00:01:52.074
One is a doubled c in one key
and a single c in the other.

00:01:52.074 --> 00:01:54.798
Two rare signs appear in only one.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.173
Found separately, a month
apart, they are the same key.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.458
Now the King's terms can be read.
Siena is to join the Holy League,

00:02:13.458 --> 00:02:15.121
at half the Pope's share.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.913
Lend the King 5,000 ducats, to
be repaid within two months.

00:02:20.913 --> 00:02:23.307
Make ready the guns at Talamone.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:29.113
And make war on X around the bridge
at Valiano, without any help.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.231
The cipher never names X, the League's enemy.

00:02:34.231 --> 00:02:39.543
And the code for whoever guarantees
the loan, M.X., is still unidentified.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.675
Two codebreakers, one key, and an emperor's
terms, read again after 530 years.

